WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.470
Ships and buried pipelines
often have blocks of zinc or

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.690
magnesium bolted onto them.

3
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.370
Over the years, those blocks
slowly corrode away and have to be

4
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.490
replaced.

5
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:11.710
Nobody minds.

6
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.190
In fact, that is the whole idea.

7
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.310
So why would engineers let one
metal be eaten away to save

8
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:18.330
another?

9
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:22.110
In this mission, you'll find out
exactly what iron needs before

10
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:23.050
it will rust.

11
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.650
You'll see how barriers such as paint,

12
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.150
oil and grease keep rust away.

13
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:31.510
Then you'll meet galvanising
and sacrificial protection,

14
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.170
where a second metal
does the protecting.

15
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:38.490
Your mission: explain why a
block of zinc can save a ship.
